WEBVTT

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:06.810
Heart rate dropping.

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:09.070
Systolic blood pressure under 70.

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:12.450
GCS 6. She's going into shock!

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:14.070
Prepare for a full-body scan.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:17.030
We might need to take emergency measures.

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:18.080
Prepare operation room 3!

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:19.620
Akane!

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:22.710
The Alone...

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:28.090
Don't worry about it! Just leave it to us!

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.340
Her level of consciousness is dropping!

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:36.470
Charge the defibrillator! Get some blood ready!

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:44.140
Akane's gonna be okay... right?

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:45.940
She'll be fine. I'm sure of it.

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:48.190
She's our Akane after all.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:55.700
She was taken into intensive care.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:58.030
What about the Alone?

00:00:59.240 --> 00:00:59.950
Huh?

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:01.910
It's on the Sky Tree?!

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:51.730
It's regenerating inside that?

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:58.400
Command to Valkyrie 1.

00:02:58.400 --> 00:02:59.950
UGVs positioned.

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:01.740
The operation will commence shortly.

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:03.660
This is Valkyrie 1. Roger.

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:05.370
Commencing observation.

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:12.380
The strong electromagnetic field around the Alone renders computer-controlled missiles and bombs useless.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:15.630
We can only rely on kinetic energy weapons.

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:30.640
A barrier?!

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:45.530
What devastating power!

00:03:55.500 --> 00:04:00.210
The enemy is protected by a barrier which UDF weapons cannot easily penetrate.

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:01.470
I see.

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:03.840
It was worth a shot anyway.

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:06.260
How's Akane?

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:10.980
The Pallet Suit protected her body from most injuries,

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:12.940
but she took a direct hit.

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:14.270
The situation is grave.

00:04:18.070 --> 00:04:19.900
Girls!

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:23.110
You can stay at the Command's dormitory.

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:24.490
Take a rest.

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:29.990
I was hospitalized for a very long time, so I know how she feels.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:35.500
The moment you first wake up in a hospital is very, very scary!

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:39.250
I want to be there for her when that moment comes.

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:41.550
I want to stay with her too.

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:43.630
It's so sad to be all alone.

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:45.340
Girls...

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:52.020
You would worry her more than help, if you exhausted yourselves like that.

00:04:57.980 --> 00:04:59.230
Okay then.

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:09.120
Momo?!

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:13.960
Sis! Sis, wake up!

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:16.120
Sis!

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:25.010
Everything was working out so well until now.

00:05:25.010 --> 00:05:29.800
I must've gotten full of myself at some point.

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:31.680
I don't think you have.

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:42.230
I looked into why Akane has to work part-time even though you hold so many patents for your inventions.

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:48.740
You gave up all that money to repent for the accident seven years ago.

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:53.370
It's mere complacency.

00:05:58.370 --> 00:05:59.250
Say,

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:03.130
why are the Alones doing stuff like this?

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:07.220
All that's certain is that they're our enemies

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:11.890
and we must use all of our power to stop them.

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:13.260
But why?

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:17.270
I've never been this afraid before...

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:24.940
Himawari...

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:42.920
It was found after yesterday's battle.

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:46.300
It should've disappeared when the transformation was canceled though...

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:52.600
This is Akane's soul!

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:58.350
It's full of her desire to protect!

00:06:59.020 --> 00:07:00.850
That's why it wouldn't disappear.

00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:05.150
<i>Akane, you're still fighting, aren't you?</i>

00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:13.030
The unknown object, called an "Alone", is currently attached to the Sky Tree, but is inactive.

00:07:13.030 --> 00:07:13.910
<i>Hatch already! This is our chance!</i>

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:17.200
The surrounding area is in chaos.

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:24.540
<i>Having a leisurely rest?</i>

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:28.050
<i>I hope you do not believe we have already won.</i>

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:31.340
I've finally got rid of one of those nuisances!

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:33.390
It should work out this time!

00:07:33.390 --> 00:07:36.640
<i>But you've only defeated </i>one<i> of them.</i>

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:39.060
This is Odaiba.

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:45.770
The injured from last night's chaos have been taken to the UDF Hospital.

00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:49.570
Understood. I'll look out for the other three too.

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:52.450
This is the current situation.

00:07:53.030 --> 00:07:55.700
Its volume has been increasing since last night.

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:59.450
We believe it's regenerating itself inside that cocoon.

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:04.960
Also, there is a strong electromagnetic field within a 500 meter radius around the cocoon

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:08.710
that disables the use of any and all electronic devices within the area.

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:13.590
But we were able to move around it just fine last night!

00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:19.810
That's because the Pallet Suits are designed differently than conventional electronics.

00:08:20.470 --> 00:08:22.310
That's all there is to it.

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:24.350
Is that all?

00:08:24.690 --> 00:08:29.610
Even if you can move about, the Pallet Suits alone can't endure the power of that beam.

00:08:29.610 --> 00:08:30.740
You're done for if you get hit.

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:32.150
Dr. Isshiki!

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:35.360
My Naked Collider's shield should be able to...

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:38.740
Even that would only last a few seconds at best.

00:08:38.740 --> 00:08:39.990
But...

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:45.370
Judging by its current growth rate, we believe that the cocoon will hatch by next morning.

00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:47.840
If that happens, we'll have no way of stopping it.

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:49.000
That doesn't even matter.

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:51.590
We already have no way to stop it.

00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:56.640
The Vivid System is the only thing that can stand up against the Alones.

00:08:56.970 --> 00:09:02.980
However, the chance of winning against this Alone without Docking is less than one percent.

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:06.520
We can't send you into such a hopeless fight!

00:09:07.230 --> 00:09:11.480
But can't I just dock with Wakaba, or something?

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:14.030
That's impossible due to the construction of the system.

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:19.910
I'm sorry, Shijou, but this is all I can do.

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:24.870
Understood. We'll end this by our own means.

00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:33.300
We recommend a saturation attack using SGE bombs.

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:33.880
What?

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:43.930
If we deploy all of the 109 bombs the UDF locked away right outside the electromagnetic field’s 500 meter radius,

00:09:43.930 --> 00:09:49.190
there’s a four percent chance the target will be eliminated.

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:50.650
Four?!

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:52.650
That's still quite an optimistic calculation.

00:09:52.650 --> 00:09:54.650
Are you out of your mind, Shijou?

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:58.240
Just one of those bombs can cause terrible destruction!

00:09:58.240 --> 00:10:01.910
Have you forgotten why the SGE bombs were locked away in the first place?

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:07.500
The damage to the atmosphere and the surrounding area would be irreversible!

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:09.000
We know.

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:13.050
Therefore, we propose the destruction of Tokyo as well.

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:16.550
So you're telling us to abandon Tokyo?!

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:18.510
If the Manifestor Engine gets destroyed,

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:21.260
the global energy supply will be cut off,

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:23.310
and the world will fall into a state of chaos.

00:10:23.810 --> 00:10:28.690
Furthermore, it's suspected that all of the Engine's energy will be released in an instant,

00:10:28.690 --> 00:10:30.520
causing unimaginable levels of destruction.

00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:33.360
Can't those girls do anything?

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:34.820
Isn't there any other way?

00:10:34.820 --> 00:10:36.280
If there was, we would've used it already!

00:10:38.240 --> 00:10:40.410
Mr. President, I need your decision.

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:44.870
We've got no choice.

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:49.040
Today at noon, an evacuation order was issued for all 23 districts of Tokyo

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:52.540
as well as the cities of Urayasu, Ichikawa, and Matsudo in the Chiba prefecture,

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:59.510
and Misato, Souka, Yashio, and Kawaguchi in the Saitama prefecture.

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:07.430
<i>There's a high chance that the red one was taken here.</i>

00:11:07.430 --> 00:11:09.890
<i>The others might be here as well.</i>

00:11:09.890 --> 00:11:10.980
Kuroki?

00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:22.200
Well,

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:29.410
I'm here because my dad's providing planes for the evacuation.

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:30.790
I see...

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:34.250
What are you doing here, Kuroki?

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:36.340
Just taking a walk...

00:11:38.090 --> 00:11:41.380
You surprised us by leaving so suddenly yesterday.

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:43.840
I remembered something really important.

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:46.350
Something important?

00:11:47.470 --> 00:11:50.850
Like, my reason to live.

00:11:52.230 --> 00:11:55.360
I see. Akane was really worried about you.

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:59.570
She was worried? But I crushed that tomato she treasured so much!

00:12:00.110 --> 00:12:02.570
You must've had your reasons.

00:12:02.570 --> 00:12:05.120
If so, she'll forgive you.

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:08.620
Whatever the reason is?

00:12:10.450 --> 00:12:11.080
Yeah.

00:12:11.790 --> 00:12:16.630
If she understands why your reason was important, she will.

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:20.630
In fact, she'll even support it.

00:12:20.630 --> 00:12:22.050
She'd tell you to do your best.

00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:27.470
Akane always gives us that supporting push.

00:12:27.470 --> 00:12:32.230
She kept telling me to do my best and that it'll work out, even when I was uncertain.

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:37.150
Do you have something important you must do as well?

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:38.940
Yeah.

00:12:40.820 --> 00:12:43.030
Let's both do our best.

00:12:44.950 --> 00:12:45.530
Yeah.

00:12:55.330 --> 00:13:00.550
<i>Akane's been supporting me ever since we've met.</i>

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:06.800
<i>She's annoying, noisy, and a real pain in the neck.</i>

00:13:07.300 --> 00:13:11.020
<i>She's an airhead that can't even fix a camera even though she's Dr. Isshiki's granddaughter.</i>

00:13:12.100 --> 00:13:12.810
<i>But...</i>

00:13:13.810 --> 00:13:17.940
<i>It's thanks to her that I could once again believe in people.</i>

00:13:18.860 --> 00:13:20.690
<i>I won't back down.</i>

00:13:24.190 --> 00:13:27.070
<i>You taught me what true strength is.</i>

00:13:29.410 --> 00:13:30.450
<i>And...</i>

00:13:31.330 --> 00:13:32.200
<i>I'm...</i>

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:34.830
Akane's friend!

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:48.510
I'm off.

00:13:49.090 --> 00:13:50.800
You're up early, Aoi.

00:13:53.850 --> 00:13:55.680
Wakaba! Himawari!

00:13:56.390 --> 00:13:57.310
Where are you headed?

00:13:59.020 --> 00:14:01.070
Um, Tokyo.

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:03.610
We've got a tour suggestion for you.

00:14:03.610 --> 00:14:04.740
Interested?

00:14:09.490 --> 00:14:12.280
We've finished loading all the SGE bombs.

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:13.830
Roger.

00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:16.580
We're deploying in five minutes.

00:14:16.580 --> 00:14:18.960
I'm sorry you have to carry out such a mission.

00:14:19.380 --> 00:14:22.880
If I think about how much those girls had to endure...

00:14:26.170 --> 00:14:27.170
The sunrise.

00:14:29.220 --> 00:14:29.970
Look!

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:50.160
Girls...

00:14:53.030 --> 00:14:54.030
But why?

00:14:57.580 --> 00:14:59.290
We'll fight too!

00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:28.900
We've got less than an hour until the predicted time of hatching.

00:15:29.610 --> 00:15:34.030
With your plan, the chance of success is slim, but it's a chance nonetheless.

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:37.410
<i>If we miss the timing, it'll be all over.</i>

00:15:37.410 --> 00:15:40.000
<i>Do you still want to do it?</i>

00:15:40.620 --> 00:15:41.330
Yes.

00:15:42.210 --> 00:15:44.750
A slight chance is better than none!

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:49.050
You thought of this plan before we did, didn't you?

00:15:50.840 --> 00:15:54.050
You have only one chance. We're counting on you three.

00:15:54.510 --> 00:15:57.930
Not just three. Akane's with us too!

00:15:59.350 --> 00:16:00.430
I see.

00:16:01.440 --> 00:16:04.270
Then we're counting on you four!

00:16:04.270 --> 00:16:05.150
Yeah!

00:16:20.250 --> 00:16:23.170
Those lights... They've really come!

00:16:23.540 --> 00:16:31.550
The core element of the plan is to attack the Alone when it opens up its barrier to attack.

00:16:32.090 --> 00:16:35.050
It takes 0.5 seconds for it to close again.

00:16:35.470 --> 00:16:38.350
That minuscule gap is the key of victory.

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:39.060
Listen!

00:16:39.600 --> 00:16:43.060
<i>First, Aoi will attack with her hammer.</i>

00:16:43.390 --> 00:16:46.270
<i>The Alone will then counterattack with its beam.</i>

00:16:46.270 --> 00:16:49.070
<i>At that moment, the barrier will be opened.</i>

00:16:49.360 --> 00:16:52.030
<i>You'll have to avoid the beam.</i>

00:16:52.030 --> 00:16:54.570
<i>It will continuously fire beams at you,</i>

00:16:54.950 --> 00:16:58.080
<i>but the hole opened from the first attack won't close.</i>

00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:01.080
<i>That's when your turn comes in, Himawari.</i>

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:04.830
<i>You'll have to prevent the hole from closing using the Collider.</i>

00:17:05.210 --> 00:17:07.380
<i>But you can only hold it open for about three seconds.</i>

00:17:07.380 --> 00:17:10.590
<i>During that time, the Alone will be defenseless.</i>

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:15.510
You'll have to attack through the opening and finish it once and for all, Wakaba.

00:17:15.510 --> 00:17:20.640
<i>You'll need to pierce through the cocoon and push the SGE bomb into its body!</i>

00:17:20.640 --> 00:17:21.470
Yes!

00:17:21.770 --> 00:17:24.480
<i>It's been modified to withstand the electromagnetic shock waves.</i>

00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:26.480
<i>It's your one and only shot.</i>

00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:30.610
If any of us misses our timing, we're all as good as dead.

00:17:30.610 --> 00:17:33.490
We really have to work in unison.

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:35.070
It's okay.

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:37.360
We can do it. I know we can.

00:17:37.780 --> 00:17:39.620
Yeah! We can!

00:17:41.290 --> 00:17:42.120
Let's do this,

00:17:42.910 --> 00:17:44.040
Akane!

00:17:47.540 --> 00:17:51.130
Okay! Commence Operation Cocoon Break!

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:52.130
Roger!

00:17:59.010 --> 00:18:00.890
<i>Are you going to use it now?</i>

00:18:01.310 --> 00:18:05.390
<i>If you use it before it hatches, it will not be at its full potential.</i>

00:18:05.890 --> 00:18:07.810
It's all in vain if they destroy it now though!

00:18:07.810 --> 00:18:09.860
I'll use another arrow if I must!

00:18:20.070 --> 00:18:22.080
Don't tell me it's already hatching!

00:18:22.490 --> 00:18:24.910
Naked Impact!

00:18:36.630 --> 00:18:37.300
Now!

00:18:49.230 --> 00:18:50.600
Wakaba!

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:01.450
Take this!

00:19:06.290 --> 00:19:07.120
Wakaba!

00:19:13.750 --> 00:19:15.670
Wakaba! Himawari!

00:19:43.030 --> 00:19:44.530
No way...

00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:47.160
It hatched!

00:19:53.420 --> 00:19:55.170
Are you okay, Wakaba?

00:19:57.550 --> 00:19:58.670
Get it together!

00:20:03.260 --> 00:20:04.640
Oh no! It's gonna shoot!

00:20:05.010 --> 00:20:06.760
Stop!

00:20:10.890 --> 00:20:13.150
<i>No! I'm not gonna make it!</i>

00:20:13.730 --> 00:20:14.900
<i>It's okay!</i>

00:21:01.650 --> 00:21:03.030
Aoi...

00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:04.450
Aoi.

00:21:09.910 --> 00:21:12.410
Thanks, Akane!

00:21:45.860 --> 00:21:47.410
I'm back!

00:21:47.700 --> 00:21:50.120
Akane!

00:21:51.660 --> 00:21:53.120
I'm fine now.

00:21:53.120 --> 00:21:54.160
Really?

00:21:54.160 --> 00:21:55.330
It doesn't hurt anywhere?

00:21:56.750 --> 00:21:59.040
I'm sorry that I made you all worry...

00:22:02.130 --> 00:22:03.260
Akane...

00:22:04.920 --> 00:22:05.880
Aoi...

00:22:07.220 --> 00:22:10.970
Akane... I did my best...

00:22:11.350 --> 00:22:12.140
Yeah...

00:22:13.930 --> 00:22:15.930
I did my best!

00:24:13.300 --> 00:24:15.800
Himawari was recruited to become a model!

00:24:15.800 --> 00:24:17.220
I'll be your manager!

00:24:17.220 --> 00:24:19.890
Let's show the world how cute you are.

00:24:19.890 --> 00:24:22.810
Next time: Sunny Sometimes Fluffy

00:24:22.810 --> 00:24:25.940
What? Why are you mad?
